From 951124c7b4dcd8e34b0580585a25d9aa981fce45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pocket-ui <noreply@pocket-ui.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:04:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] apu: the DSP preference set on each new APU state, not cached
 in a static; sound after a relaunch in the libretro core

mcpx_apu_update_dsp_preference cached the preference it last applied in a
function-local static and returned early while it matched. The APU state
is allocated afresh at each boot (nc_dev_apu_init, zeroed pages), and the
libretro core boots again in its frontend's process for a reset or a
title's relaunch (XLaunchNewImage, boot_again). There the static still
matched, so the new state kept monitor.point 0, MCPX_APU_DEBUG_MON_AC97:
the VP's mix was not copied into the output frame and the EP's samples
were refused. The output ring was fed zeros from then on, the stream to
the frontend running but silent. Jade Empire lost music, speech and
effects at its relaunch into default.xbe after New Game (about 50 s in,
Retroid Pocket Mini V2, ROCKNIX, RetroArch). Android is not affected: its
core runs once per process.

The preference is now set on the state every time (three stores a frame),
so a new state always gets it and a change still takes effect at the next
frame.

apu-reinit-smoke makes and frees the APU five times in one process with
each preference twice in a row, checks the monitor point and the DSPs'
realtime flags, and sends a known EP frame through the libretro output.

Analysis and test: Sol (code review) and Claude (device trace).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
